  "title": "Synthetic Data for OCR Transfer in Thai Documents",
  "summary": "arXiv AI and arXiv Computer Vision reports on synthetic OCR training for Thai OCR systems, addressing issues like realism and transferability. Synthetic data provide exact labels but struggle with domain drift and context, while controlled pipelines improve transfer performance.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Synthetic data provide exact labels at scale, but'realism' conflates source domain, page context, typography, spatial structure, and glyph variation.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "We disentangle these factors with a controlled document-reconstruction pipeline and evaluate each variant under page- and crop-level training.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Wayu-Paxa-OCR-Zero, a Thai OCR model, achieves competitive performance with synthetic-only training.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
